Desktop Name Manager @VERSION@: the menu-bar app, and the `dnm` command-line tool (also installed as `desktop-name`).

@NOTES@

## Install

```sh
brew tap inquinity/tap
brew trust --tap inquinity/tap   # Homebrew 7 and later load casks only from taps you trust
brew install --cask inquinity/tap/desktop-name-manager
```

macOS 27 or later, Apple silicon only. The app is notarized and the ticket is stapled to it, so it passes
macOS's check without a network connection; neither the app nor `dnm` ever connects to the network.

